## Capture the question

A useful development note begins with a specific question. What was confusing? What did you expect to happen? What actually happened?

## Keep a small example

Reduce the problem until the important behaviour is visible. A short example often teaches more than a long description of an entire application.

## Write the next step

End with something testable: a change to try, a measurement to take or a new question. A notebook becomes useful when it helps you resume work.

